// Hand-curated position characteristics (position_rules_sets) for the rules
// sets no importer can supply correctly.
//
// This file lives in after-other-importers, never before, and that is load
// bearing: PositionRulesSetsService.sync matches by the natural key
// (position_id, rules_set_id) and updates in place, and the BBL importer can
// assign its single BB2020-snapshot stat line to an older rules set whenever
// it finds real usage evidence there. Curating before the importers would let
// that snapshot overwrite these values on the very same key; curating after
// means these values win.
//
// CRP, CRP+ and BB2016 declare passingFormat: 'absent' (see
// data/before-other-importers/spp-award-values.json5), so their entries omit
// `passing` entirely -- the processor sends the omission on as an explicit
// null and the API rejects a value here. BB2020 entries must carry `passing`.
//
// Every `position` id is the "Name" external id
// NameExternalIdService.forPosition builds -- "<raceName>: <positionName>" for
// a regular position, the bare name for a star player -- taken verbatim from
// the imported database, not from the rulebook's own spelling.
//
// Sources, per rules set:
//   CRP    -- m750496a_BB_Competition_Rules_Pack.pdf, roster pages 23-25.
//   CRP    -- Stunty_Leeg_Handbook_v1_0.pdf, pages 8-11, for the Stunty Leeg
//             teams the main CRP book does not list.
//   CRP+   -- NTBB2015.pdf ("Narrow-Tier Blood Bowl 2015"), pages 3-8.
//   BB2016 -- BB-Teams-of-Legend-Revised-1.pdf, plus values transcribed from
//             the physical rulebooks where no PDF covers them.
//   BB2020 -- gap-filling only, for pairs the BBL/TP importers left with no
//             row at all.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' },
  ],
  positionRulesSets: [
    // --- CRP: Dark Elf (CRP p.23) ---
